WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.357
Good morning!

2
00:00:02.358 --> 00:00:05.299
Who are

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:11.811
you? I'm a

4
00:00:11.812 --> 00:00:14.862
groundhog. Groundhogs are

5
00:00:14.863 --> 00:00:18.857
big rodents. We're also

6
00:00:18.858 --> 00:00:23.910
called woodchucks. Where do

7
00:00:23.911 --> 00:00:26.110
you live? We live

8
00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:30.168
near fields and meadows. We usually

9
00:00:30.169 --> 00:00:35.061
stay close to forests. What do

10
00:00:35.062 --> 00:00:37.283
you eat? We

11
00:00:37.284 --> 00:00:41.713
like grasses, plants, and fruit. Sometimes

12
00:00:41.714 --> 00:00:47.644
we eat tree bark or bugs too. You

13
00:00:47.645 --> 00:00:50.270
eat a lot! We

14
00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:54.267
eat a lot in summer and fall. But

15
00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:58.834
we don't eat during winter. Groundhogs

16
00:00:58.835 --> 00:01:04.592
hibernate all winter long. Do

17
00:01:04.593 --> 00:01:08.048
you ever climb trees? Yes.

18
00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:13.013
We climb trees and bushes. We

19
00:01:13.014 --> 00:01:16.560
can swim too. Who

20
00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:19.456
are your enemies? Bears

21
00:01:19.457 --> 00:01:23.349
and foxes hunt us. So

22
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.895
do wolves and birds. We

23
00:01:26.896 --> 00:01:31.312
hide from enemies underground.

24
00:01:31.313 --> 00:01:34.407
Do you dig holes?

25
00:01:34.408 --> 00:01:39.059
Yes! Groundhogs are good diggers.

26
00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.212
We use our claws to dig deep holes.

27
00:01:43.213 --> 00:01:49.402
Our holes have rooms and tunnels.

28
00:01:49.403 --> 00:01:53.032
Here comes a fox.

29
00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:56.409
Time to hide!

30
00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:00.825
Good-bye, Groundhog!

